{comment: Verse 1}
You are [C]standing on the mountain holding [F]to the Shepherd's [C]hand
The [Em]valley you just [Am]came through, was [D]hard to under[G]stand
Then the [C]Shepherd draws you [C7]closer
There's something [F]He wants you to [Bb]see
And He [C/G]points back [E/Ab]to the  [Am]valley and [Dm7]unfolds its [G]myste[C]ries[Gsus4]

{comment: Verse 2}
As the [C]eagles soar [C7]around you and you look [F]back on where you've [C]been
One by [Em]one He answers [Am]questions, that He [D]did not answer [G]then
He [C]now shows you the [C7]danger, of [F]going your own [Bb]way
All those [C/G]roads you [E/Ab]thought were [Am]better
Would have [Dm7]led your [G]soul as[C]tray[Gsus4]

{comment: Verse 3}
He[C] reminds you of that [C7]moment, when you [F]could not make it [C]through
Now you [Em]see one set of [Am]footprints where He reached [D]down and carried [G]you
As your [C]tears fall on His [C7]shoulder, and you [F]thank Him for His [Bb]love
He says "[C/G]Child, I [E/Ab]knew that [Am]one day, you'd see [Dm]this valley [G]from a[C]bove"[G]

{comment: Verse 4}
Things look [C]different on the mountain from the [F]Shepherd's [G]point of [C]view[G]
Standing [C]high above the [Am]trial, that He [D]brought you safely [G]through
All the [C]valley's disap[CM7]pointments, will [Gm]never [C]look the [F]same to you[Bb]
For things look [C]different [E/Ab]on the  [Am]mountain
